Rule 1 (If input is float32, max must be float32 or float64)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 8 then dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9
>>
Rule 2 (If max is a tensor, it must have the same number of dimensions as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (if max is a tensor, the shapes of input and max must be broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
